Local modifications to the vendored linter are marked inline in the source and
listed in skills/human-writing/references/maintenance.md under "Local deltas
against upstream" and "Provenance". There are three: the em-dash check fires on
presence rather than upstream's density gate, additive pattern entries in
ai_prose_patterns.json, and one user-facing path string in patterns.py corrected to
name a file that exists (2026-09-17).

===============================================================================
2. JCarterJohnson/vibecoded-design-tells, pinned f7c4aef (2026-06-23)
   Covers: skills/human-writing/references/tells.md (Parts A-C) and
   references/writing-with-intent.md, which came here with the former unslop-text
   skill when it moved from Packs/unslop on 2026-07-25; and skills/unslop/
   (SKILL.md, references/, scripts/), which came here whole when the unslop Pack was
   merged into this one on 2026-09-17.
   https://github.com/JCarterJohnson/vibecoded-design-tells
===============================================================================

One upstream, one notice, covering both halves of it. The unslop skill was adapted
near-verbatim from the same pinned commit, so its former Pack-level LICENSE carried the
identical grant text and is now this section — nothing was dropped in the merge. Its local
deltas are recorded in skills/unslop/SKILL.md and in this pack's README: each description
had a small number of second-person clauses reworded to clear the third-person discovery
convention; references/ is renamed only (tells.md -> tells-code.md / tells-ui.md); and six
user-facing strings in scripts/ were corrected on 2026-09-17, because the 2026-07-28 rename
left them pointing at `references/tells.md`, a path that no longer exists.

