documentation vendored into skills/, not any raw harvested dataset, since none
was vendored.

===============================================================================
3. ryanthedev/oberskills, pinned 5050537 (v2.8.1, 2026-07-25): credited, not vendored
   https://github.com/ryanthedev/oberskills
===============================================================================

The architecture of skills/human-writing (its mode router, reader-job taxonomy,
voice-profile pattern, and review protocol) was informed by the `write` skill in
this repo. No text or code was copied: references/types.md and
references/voice-template.md are rewritten from scratch and each carries an
explicit note saying so.

This matters because that repo declares MIT in .claude-plugin/plugin.json only and
ships no LICENSE file at its root, so the grant is thinner than the two above. The
paraphrase-only treatment is deliberate: ideas and structure are not the subject of
copyright, so nothing here depends on that declaration holding. Revisit if upstream
adds a proper LICENSE file.

===============================================================================
4. skill-creator, and everything else original to this pack
===============================================================================

MIT, same terms as above, per Packs/writing/pack.toml.

Also here without a notice obligation, all three recorded in upstreams.toml where their
verdicts live: `skill-creator`'s sources (Anthropic's docs and the agentskills.io spec,
absorbed as rules rather than text, plus a third-party PDF carried idea-only);
`academic-writing`, whose upstreams are `[research-paper-writing-skills]`,
`[academic-writing-agents]` and `[pengsida-research-notes]`, all verdict `quarry` with no
grant of any kind, so nothing was copied and everything taken was paraphrased; and the
`unslop` descriptions' reworded clauses noted in section 2.
